      "writtenOn": "2020-09-21T19:41:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e wouldn\u0027t this require USE_GOMA to still work?\n\nInternally, yes. When a user sets `USE_GOMA\u003dtrue`, it will be caught in the block above this and the build would fail right away. If the user were to set `FORCE_USE_GOMA`, then we would set `USE_GOMA\u003dtrue` here and the build would continue as if the user actually set `USE_GOMA`.\n\nIf we were to actually do a string replace of USE_GOMA with FORCE_USE_GOMA, we would also have to make changes to kati since some makefile to ninja file translation also have USE_GOMA hardcoded there (https://github.com/google/kati/blob/631e467325a191a92d2e9454dc9b0fe6e3f21f80/src/ninja.cc#L189). The build actually fails without the kati change.\n\nI figured this would be a simpler change that achieves the same purpose.",
      "parentUuid": "dcf02bb8_d2b77b6d",
